;; The dictionary the browser suite serves (#289). Built into
;; target/test-dictionary by `clojure -X:dictionary-fixture`, served by a
;; backend started with LEARNING_APP__DICTIONARY_DIR.
;;
;; Why not the shipped dictionary: it is 37 MB, every Playwright test gets a
;; fresh context, and the SQLite worker imports the whole file into an empty
;; OPFS before the first suggestion can appear.
;;
;; Two properties the specs depend on — do not break them casually:
;;
;;   - every prefix of "Fenster" (f, fe, fen, fens, fenst, fenste, fenster)
;;     matches at least one surface form, so the list opens once and never
;;     collapses mid-word: one clean open to measure;
;;   - "fenster" matches exactly two lemmas, which is how a spec tells this
;;     fixture apart from the shipped dictionary. Forget the environment
;;     variable and the suite fails loudly instead of quietly crawling.
;;
;;   - "ruecken" is one lemma exactly, der Rücken, and it is outranked by its
;;     compound das Rückenmark; that is what lets a spec see an exact match
;;     come first rather than merely rank first (#357).
;;
;; Shape is what dictionary.materialize/build-table-data consumes. Surface
;; forms are derived from :value and :forms by the same materializer the real
;; build runs, so normalization can never drift from what the client queries.
;; Ranks are distinct: ordering is exact matches first, then `rank DESC, value ASC`.
[{:value        "das Fenster"
  :pos          "noun"
  :rank         900
  :forms        ["Fensters" "Fenstern"]
  :translations [{:lang "ru" :value "окно"}]}

